(7761064, 1285503, 88235, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> I recall many drives across the old Tappan Zee when I was a kid, but I don''t live there anymore and haven''t been across this new one. I''ll be about 10 miles from it next week for work. Is there a good perspective from the banks? Although it appears there may be a ped/bike lane on this new bridge to get out on it. Maybe worth a short drive if I have the time. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Either side has a good perspective from the banks. Though the east side is much closer to the center span and is more dramatic. There is a bike / pedestrian path across the bridge with a couple of resting spots where you can stop and enjoy the river. Free parking on either side. <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: I recall many drives across the old Tappan Zee when I was a kid, but I don''t live there anymore and haven''t been across this new one. I''ll be about 10 miles from it next week for work. Is there a good perspective from the banks? Although it appears there may be a ped/bike lane on this new bridge to get out on it. Maybe worth a short drive if I have the time.   Either side has a good perspective from the banks. Though the east side is much closer to the center span and is more dramatic. There is a bike / pedestrian path across the bridge with a couple of resting spots where you can stop and enjoy the river. Free parking on either side. ', '2023-12-15 09:02:43.000000', NULL, 0),
